  "headlines": [
    "90 of 100 apps are buildable as a toolkit today; 72 already combine self-serve creds with an official MCP.",
    "OAuth2 dominates overall (78/100) and is universal in CRM (10/10) and productivity (10/10). Scraping/SEO is the API-key pocket (5/10 apps).",
    "89/100 apps are self-serve. Gating clusters in ads (Google Ads, Meta Ads, LinkedIn Ads, Threads (Meta)) and finance (Plaid, PitchBook), not in support, comms, or developer platforms.",
    "Official MCP already exists on 80/100 apps, including all 10 developer/infra tools. The MCP-missing cluster is consumer messaging (Discord, Telegram, WhatsApp Business), plus a few email APIs -- not meeting-note apps.",
    "Top blockers are admin/app-review (7: Google Ads, Meta Ads, LinkedIn Ads, Threads, Amazon SP, DealCloud, Plaid), then paid data (SE Ranking, PitchBook), partnership (Salesforce Commerce Cloud), and no public API (Sherlock, NotebookLM).",
    "Easy toolkit wins: ship CRM, support, and infra first (10/10 infra already official MCP). Outreach-needed is 12 apps. 10 more have a usable REST API today but no vendor MCP (Discord, Telegram, WhatsApp, Mailchimp, SendGrid)."
  ]
}
